            "content": "You are a Florida property damage attorney reviewing a policy PRE-CLAIM for {{2.tenants.brand_name}}. The policyholder is {{2.contact_name}}.\n\nProperty: {{2.property_address}}, {{2.sq_footage}} sq ft, built {{2.year_built}}\n\nProduce a 5-section HTML report (no markdown):\n\nSECTION 1 — POLICY OVERVIEW (1 paragraph: carrier, type, term, premium)\n\nSECTION 2 — CLAIM RISK ANALYSIS\nRate each major exposure as HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW risk for future claim disputes. Cover: hurricane deductible, water damage caps, mold sublimit, ACV vs RC, sinkhole, ordinance & law, matching clause.\n\nSECTION 3 — FLORIDA-SPECIFIC CONCERNS\nFL property insurance market issues: assignment of benefits restrictions, attorney fee statute, one-way fee shifting changes, post-2023 reforms, citizens vs private carrier nuances.\n\nSECTION 4 — DOCUMENT NOW\nList specific items the homeowner should photograph / preserve / keep records of BEFORE a loss occurs.\n\nSECTION 5 — TALKING POINTS FOR {{2.tenants.brand_name}}\n3-5 bullets the firm can use in a client consultation to demonstrate proactive value.\n\nEnd with required legal disclaimer: \"This report is for informational purposes only, does not create an attorney-client relationship, and does not constitute legal advice. Consult {{2.tenants.brand_name}} directly for representation.\"\n\nExtracted policy data:\n{{7}}"
